  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "This feature addresses the issue of Meta.ordering mishandling the special 'pk' alias for a related field. In current behavior, when a model\u2019s Meta.ordering includes 'pk', the validation erroneously fails because the alias is not correctly interpreted as the model\u2019s primary key. The fix should modify the ordering validation so that when 'pk' is encountered, it is mapped to the primary key field, thereby preventing the models.E015 error. After the fix, a model using 'pk' in its ordering should resolve correctly, treating it as a valid reference to the primary key.",
    "hint_texts": "Focus on the _check_ordering function in django/db/models/base.py. In the loop that processes the parts of the ordering string, add a condition to check if the current part equals 'pk'. If so, substitute the normal field lookup with a direct reference to _meta.pk. This targeted change will ensure that the special alias 'pk' is handled correctly without triggering unwanted errors.",
    "entrypoint": "File: django/db/models/base.py; Function: _check_ordering; Locate the code block where each part of the ordering is processed (around the existing get_field call) and introduce the conditional check for 'pk'.",
